185	zis52	68	0	instruments_tools	The questionnaire operationalizes four dimensions of aggression physical and verbal aggression as behavioral tendencies anger as an affective component and hostility as a cognitive component. The development of the questionnaire is based on the work of Buss and Perry 1992 .
185	zis71	69	0	instruments_tools	The present questionnaire records the trend towards health related concerns. The development of the scale is based on the work of Salkovskis et al. 2002 and represents the German and abbreviated version of the scale produced by them.
185	zis193	70	0	instruments_tools	This 1 item scale measures the subjective perception of belonging to a population stratum. A distinction is made between the following population strata Working class middle class upper middle class and upper class.
185	zis365	71	0	instruments_tools	The concept addressed is perceived individual experiences of discrimination in everyday life as assessed by the Everyday Discrimination Scale. A German Arabic and Dari adaptation of the scale by Williams et al. 1997 is presented which underwent cognitive pretesting revision and validation in two samples a probability individual register sample for German and Arabic and a convenience sample recruited via Facebook for Arabic and Dari . The studies targeted the German speaking population and individuals with a migration background or refugees proficient in Arabic or Dari aged 18 years or older. Confirmatory Factor Analyses CFAs supported the unidimensional structure of the instrument. Validity and reliability analyses support its use within each language group and heterogeneous samples. Measurement invariance analyses showed that correlations can be compared without restrictions and means can be compared on the basis of partial invariance models.
185	zis50	72	0	instruments_tools	The questionnaire records the tendency towards self monitoring. In addition to an overall value the four subscales Acting Extraversion Other Directedness and Sensitivity for expressive behavior and social cues are mapped. The development of the scale is based on the work of Snyder 1974 .
185	zis178	73	0	instruments_tools	The scale measures the awareness of consequences of action on a global level with three items. This corresponds to the degree of awareness of the consequences of one s own actions for global environmental changes. The development of the scale is based on the works of Schwartz 1977 1981 .
