6171	zis343	62	0	instruments_tools	Respondents age is together with sex gender the most important socio demographic variable recorded in all surveys. Age provides information about partly biologically determined development and ageing processes and positioning in the life course. It is therefore related to a variety of socio economic characteristics but also to attitudes behaviour and in particular health. It is controlled for in practically all multivariate statistical models. In most studies the age at the time of the survey is determined using questions on the month and year of birth and published as a derived variable. Membership in a birth cohort is also derived from the year of birth. It is used to depict similar overall social living conditions and experiences that lead to the construction of generations e.g. the post war generation or the baby boomers .
