66255	zis304	24	5	instruments_tools	The Employee Experience Questionnaire EXQ is a German language measure for obtaining a wholistic picture of Employee eXperience at work. Employee experience describes major perceptions attitudes and behaviors of employees in organizations. The EXQ comprises the following four constructs job satisfaction organisational commitment individual engagement and collective engagement. The EXQ shows good psychometric properties. Substantial correlations with related constructs are indicators for both convergent as well as divergent construct validity and criterion validity of the instrument.
66255	zis343	25	5	instruments_tools	Respondents age is together with sex gender the most important socio demographic variable recorded in all surveys. Age provides information about partly biologically determined development and ageing processes and positioning in the life course. It is therefore related to a variety of socio economic characteristics but also to attitudes behaviour and in particular health. It is controlled for in practically all multivariate statistical models. In most studies the age at the time of the survey is determined using questions on the month and year of birth and published as a derived variable. Membership in a birth cohort is also derived from the year of birth. It is used to depict similar overall social living conditions and experiences that lead to the construction of generations e.g. the post war generation or the baby boomers .
66255	zis114	26	0	instruments_tools	The instrument is one of eight item batteries that Lederer used as subscales to capture various aspects of attitudes to authority. This subscale is used to record attitudes to loyalty to the state and patriotism.
